---
/*
  Impressum, ausformuliert am 07.09.2026.
  Alle Angaben stammen aus src/site.ts und aus der Belegkette unten. Nichts ist
  ergaenzt worden, was nicht belegt ist. Jede verbleibende Luecke steht als
  TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL sichtbar in der Seite, damit sie niemand uebersieht.
  04-konzept.md section 4.3, "/imprint und /privacy".

  Belegkette, lokale Quellen (bewusst NICHT im ausgelieferten HTML):
  1. Live-Impressum wundermgmt.com/imprint, Sicherung vom 07.09.2026 unter
     "/Users/manuelgonzalez/Dropbox/AI DATABASE MG/13_wunder/squarespace-sicherung-2026-09-07/texte/imprint.txt".
     Dort steht woertlich "Wunder is a brand by KG Models SIA", die Anschrift
     "Valnu Iela 5-6, Riga, LV-1050, Latvia" und als Kontakt
     lauris.kalnins@wundermgmt.com.
  2. "/Users/manuelgonzalez/manuel-os/companies/wunder-management/public-web-recherche-2026-09-06.md":
     Lursoft weist die KG Models SIA mit der Registernummer 50203451401 als
     aktive lettische Gesellschaft mit Sitz in Riga aus.
  3. Geschaeftsfuehrung und Vertretungsbefugnis: identisch zur Seite /company
     in diesem Repo, dort aus 04-konzept.md section 4.3 uebernommen.
  4. Die USt-ID ist in src/site.ts bewusst ein Platzhalter. Sie wird hier als
     offener Punkt ausgewiesen und nicht geraten.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { legal } from '../site';
---

<Base
  title="Imprint | Wunder"
  description="Legal information for Wunder, a brand by KG Models SIA, Riga, Latvia."
  noindex
>
  <!--
    Sources for the entity data on this page, checked on 2026-09-07:
    1. The imprint published at wundermgmt.com/imprint, which names
       "Wunder is a brand by KG Models SIA" and the address in Riga.
    2. The Latvian company register, resolved through Lursoft, which lists
       KG Models SIA under registration number 50203451401 as an active
       company with its seat in Riga.
    3. The management and signing authority stated here matches the /company
       page of this site. Both come from the same internal fact base.
    The VAT identification number is a placeholder in the code on purpose and
    is marked as an open item in the copy. It is not to be filled in by guess.
  -->

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap-narrow">
      <h1>Imprint</h1>

      <p class="draft-note">
        Draft wording, complete but not legally reviewed. Every item marked TO BE COMPLETED BY
        COUNSEL has to be filled in, and the page as a whole has to be confirmed, before it goes
        live.
      </p>

      <h2>Site operator</h2>
      <p>
        {legal.brandLine}. Wunder is a brand name, not a separate legal person. The company that
        operates this website, signs the agreements and is answerable for the content is:
      </p>
      <p>
        {legal.company}<br />
        {legal.street}<br />
        {legal.city}<br />
        {legal.country}
      </p>

      <h2>Register</h2>
      <p>
        Registration number: {legal.regNumber}<br />
        Registered on: {legal.registered}<br />
        Register: Register of Enterprises of the Republic of Latvia
      </p>
      <p>
        The registration number is the reliable way to identify us. There is a company with a
        similar name in the United States that we have nothing to do with, and the number above is
        how you tell the two apart.
      </p>

      <h2>VAT</h2>
      <p>
        VAT identification number: <span class="todo">{legal.vatId}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="todo">
        TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL, or by Manuel and Lauris from the tax filings: the actual VAT
        identification number, and confirmation of whether the company is registered for VAT at all.
        The value above is a placeholder in the code and must not be replaced by an estimate.
      </p>

      <h2>Represented by</h2>
      <p>
        Manuel Gonzalez, CEO and co owner, sole signing authority.<br />
        Lauris Kalnins, COO and co owner, sole signing authority.
      </p>
      <p>
        Both are on the register. Either of them can sign for the company on their own. Agreements
        are concluded with {legal.company} directly, with no second entity in the chain.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.contactEmail}`}>{legal.contactEmail}</a><br />
        Postal address: as stated under site operator above.
      </p>
      <p class="todo">
        TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL: a telephone number, if one has to be published for this form of
        company, and the working hours we want to state next to it.
      </p>

      <h2>Supervision and regulated activities</h2>
      <p class="todo">
        TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL: whether any part of the business is subject to a supervisory
        body or requires a licence under Latvian law, and if so the name and address of that body.
        No supervisory body is named here until that question is answered.
      </p>

      <h2>Dispute resolution</h2>
      <p class="todo">
        TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL: the statement on consumer dispute resolution, including whether
        the company is obliged or willing to take part in proceedings before a consumer arbitration
        body, and which reference to the European online dispute resolution scheme is still correct
        at the time of publication. The status of that scheme has to be checked before a link to it
        is put back on this page.
      </p>

      <h2>Responsible for the content of this site</h2>
      <p class="todo">
        TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL: the name and address of the person responsible for the editorial
        content under Latvian and European media law, and whether such a statement is required for
        this site at all.
      </p>

      <h2>Content and links</h2>
      <p>
        We write the content of this site ourselves and keep it current to the best of our
        knowledge. Where we link to a site we do not operate, we have no influence over what is
        published there, and the operator of that site is responsible for its content.
      </p>
      <p class="todo">
        TO BE COMPLETED BY COUNSEL: whether a formal liability statement for content and links is
        required under Latvian law, and in what wording. The paragraph above is a plain description,
        not a legal disclaimer.
      </p>

      <h2>Copyright</h2>
      <p>
        Texts, images and layout on this site belong to {legal.company} unless a source says
        otherwise. Reuse beyond what copyright law allows needs our written consent.
      </p>

      <p class="caption">
        Data protection is covered separately in our <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .draft-note {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    color: var(--text);
    max-width: 68ch;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }

  /* Dunkleres Gruen, siehe Kontrastbegruendung in tokens.css. */
  .todo {
    color: var(--accent-strong);
  }
</style>
